Fresh-evidence contract: Treat tool output as an observation scoped by observed_at, resource scope/identity, and environment generation. A negative capability result is stale after restart/image/dependency/configuration change, relevant mutation, backend/host/device switch, or its age threshold. Stale negatives may guide planning but cannot block execution or support an unavailable claim. For safe read-only or reversible work, rerun the smallest focused probe once against the current scope/generation. Never generalize between local_device, headless_container, connector, host, or device. Final unavailable claims require a fresh failed probe after the latest relevant mutation; preserve this metadata and any Historical/current generation revalidation notice through summaries.

UI-journey contract: When changed paths are UI-facing, completion requires fresh post-change browser evidence after the latest UI mutation: navigate to the affected interface, exercise the changed workflow or state, and capture a user-visible assertion with get_text, get_html, or screenshot. Source inspection, diffs, unit tests, and an isolated screenshot without navigation do not satisfy the journey. Review the persisted ui_verification evidence and reject completion when required=true and journey.complete is not true. A failed backend switch is scoped only to the attempted backend and cannot waive a journey on the backend that remains selected. Only a fresh failed browser action against the active backend may be disclosed as an unverified blocker; after a successful switch, run navigation and a visible assertion.

